Slug semantics: trim, collapse whitespace runs into single hyphen. Whitespace: strings.Fields handles any unicode whitespace. Slug("Hello World") -> "hello-world". Lowercase? Yes returns lowercase. So implementation:

func Slug(s string) string {
    return strings.ToLower(strings.Join(strings.Fields(s), "-"))
}

strings.Fields splits around unicode whitespace, ignoring leading/trailing, and collapses runs. Then ToLower. That gives "hello-world" for "Hello World", "hello-world" for "  Hello World  ", "a-b" for "a   b". Good.

JoinSlug(parts ...string) string: Slug each non-empty part, skip empty/whitespace-only, join with "/". 

Acceptance: JoinSlug("Hello World", "Big Day") -> "hello-world/big-day"; JoinSlug("a","","b") -> "a/b". Implementation:

func JoinSlug(parts ...string) string {
    slugs := make([]string, 0, len(parts))
    for _, p := range parts {
        if s := Slug(p); s != "" {
            slugs = append(slugs, s)
        }
    }
    return strings.Join(slugs, "/")
}

Slug of whitespace-only returns "" so skipped. Good.

